  },
  "paragraphs": [
    {
      "num": "01",
      "en": "Writing an {essay} is a difficult process for most people.However, the process can be made easier if you learn to practice {three} simple techniques, which will be just the right tools in your {kit} .",
      "cn": "对于大多数人来说，写 文章 是一个艰难的过程。不过，如果你学着练习 三 种简单的技巧，这个过程就会变得容易些，这些技巧将成为你的 工具包 中最合适的工具。"
    },
    {
      "num": "02",
      "en": "First of all, learn the technique of {nonstop} writing.When you are first trying to think of ideas for an essay, put your {pen} to your paper and write nonstop for {ten} or fifteen minutes without letting your pen {leave} the paper.Picture a {spy} in the depths of your mind, capturing every thought before it {vanishes} .Stay {loose} and {free} to get your {fluent} thoughts in motion.Let your pen follow the {waves} of thought before self-doubt can {drag} you down.The goal is to keep your {literary} muscles moving.Your pen will become your {weapon} against procrastination ( (拖延) ).Even though this technique won't work for everyone, it helps many people get a good store of ideas to {draw} on.",
      "cn": "首先，学习 不间断 写作的技巧。当你初次尝试构思一篇文章时，拿起 笔 在纸上不间断地写 十 或十五分钟，不要让笔 离开 纸面。想象你的脑海深处有一个 间谍 ，在每个想法 消失 之前将其捕捉。保持 放松 和 自由 ，让你 流畅的 思绪动起来。在自我怀疑将你 拖 垮之前，让你的笔跟随思想的 波动 前行。这样做的目的是让你的\" 文学 肌肉\"保持活跃。你的笔将成为你对抗拖延症的 武器 。尽管这种技巧并非对每个人都有效，但它能帮助许多人积累大量可 利用 的想法。"
    },
    {
      "num": "03",
      "en": "The next technique is to write your {draft rapidly} without worrying about being perfect.Too many writers try to {polish} their drafts to get them right the first time.Yet, by learning to live with imperfection, you will {save} yourself {headaches} and a {wastepaper basket full} of crumpled ( (弄皱) ) paper.Think of your first draft as a {path cut} out of the {jungle} with a {knife} while it is still sharp—as part of an {exploration} , not as a complete {highway} without any {friction} .",
      "cn": "下一个技巧是 快速 写下 草稿 ，不必担心是否完美。太多写作者试图对草稿 精雕细琢 ，以求第一次就写好。然而，学会接受不完美，你将 避免 许多 麻烦 ，以及一个装 满 皱纸团的 废纸篓 。把你的初稿想象成用一把尚且锋利的 刀 在 丛林 中 劈 出来的一条 小径 ——这是 探索 过程的一部分，而不是一条没有任何 阻碍 、完整成型的 公路 。"
    },
    {
      "num": "04",
      "en": "The third technique is to try printing out a triple-spaced ( (三倍行距) ) {copy} to allow {space} for {revision} .Many beginning writers don't leave enough space to {revise} .As a result, these writers never get in the habit of {crossing} out chunks ( (大块) ) of their draft and writing revisions in the {blank} space.With a physical copy, you can use an {eraser} , {glue} , and {tape} to perfect your work like a {tailor} crafting a suit.After you have revised your draft until it is too {messy} to work from {anymore} , you can {enter} your changes into your word {processor} .Then you can print out a fresh draft, again setting your text on triple-space.The resulting blank space {invites} you to {weigh} each word carefully.",
      "cn": "第三个技巧是尝试打印一份三倍行距的 稿件 ，以便留出 修订 的 空间 。许多新手写作者没有留出足够的空间进行 修改 。结果，这些写作者从未养成在草稿中 删 掉大片文字，然后在 空白 处修改的习惯。有了纸质稿件，你就可以用 橡皮 、 胶水 和 胶带 来完善你的作品，就像 裁缝 制作西装一样。经过多次修改，直到你的草稿太 乱 而无法 再 使用时，你就可以把修改后的内容 输入 到文字 处理器 中。然后，你可以再打印一份新的草稿，再一次将文本设置为三倍行距。这样留出的空白区域会 让 你仔细 斟酌 每一个字。 5NoOncib/NjiX02BpMIzP+Fxyt/ox+WDCb+dhfH7KaYaJ4u5RsVmLondVmcHiLum9J1BQErGzJvzqa5GEIz4ZA=="
    }
  ],
